        "blocking": false,
        "finding": "The justification of this FUNCTIONAL_TEST obligation announces \"Execute the documentary scenarios, observable markup contract and preservation checks\", but its `expected` (and the paired TEST-b9c00e5c0d8233c519d2614f) contains only the toggle transitions, the sentinel preservation block and the subprocess isolation rules — no markup assertion. The markup contract appears only in the other two plan items' obligations. Nothing is actually lost, because all three test obligations compose one tests/ui.test.js delivery, but the justification overstates the scope of this proof and could lead an implementer or an implementation reviewer to look for markup evidence under CRT-ed0bc0861767a4340ce36114, whose only assertion is the Boolean toggle return value.",
        "evidence": [
          "CRT-ed0bc0861767a4340ce36114 — single assertion AST-11fc56765512d7c9720467da, property_type STATE, subject \"src/features/example/Screen.js#toggle() return value\", proof_required [\"FUNCTIONAL_TEST\"]",
          "PROOF-4e3f335329f63eec7b0e37d8.expected and TEST-b9c00e5c0d8233c519d2614f.expected — contain only the toggle/sentinel/isolation text, unlike TEST-f1b692f59ec2f3530f895873 and TEST-6fd8a43c2b71b836def3e99a which carry the render()/402px/874px/title assertions",
          "PROOF-4e3f335329f63eec7b0e37d8.justification: \"Execute the documentary scenarios, observable markup contract and preservation checks; rendered geometry is measured by the separate VISUAL_COMPARE observer.\""
        ],
        "required_correction": "Align the justification of PROOF-4e3f335329f63eec7b0e37d8 with its expected text by removing \"observable markup contract\", or state explicitly that the markup contract is delivered by the shared tests/ui.test.js and proven under PROOF-ae75bb1199c4d5d2d68ef93a and PROOF-1062ab648833d3513c8af136.",
        "dependency_target_ids": [
