      {
        "finding_id": "FND-da57bc923f558e81d48c6194",
        "category": "PLAN_GAP",
        "target_type": "PLAN_CONTRACT",
        "target_id": "b7276ce02c24e3fc55331b86b8d997287cf9890547a46eb9572140238c124e06",
        "blocking": true,
        "finding": "The plan requires \"explicit fixed CSS width:402px and height:874px\" and that frame 4478:7209 \"must explicitly use box-sizing:border-box, border:0 and padding:0\", but no constraint states WHERE those declarations must live. The post-delivery markup gate reads them from one place only: it scans the render() string for the first tag bearing data-figma-id=\"4478:7209\", requires a style=\"...\" attribute ON THAT TAG, and parses width/height from that attribute. A delivery that declares the identical fixed geometry in a <style> block or a CSS class inside the returned markup renders at exactly 402x874 (the host page zeroes html/body margins, so rendered geometry is identical) and therefore satisfies both VISUAL_COMPARE obligations and the rendered-geometry wording of the plan, yet is rejected with VNEXT_FIGMA_REAL_DIMENSION_DECLARATIONS_REQUIRED before any review verdict. The plan as written admits a conforming delivery that the gate refuses.",
        "evidence": [
          "CHG-c9625c383df5de1cd29b7051 / IMP-229b28a0d2ccd5de1d43304c intent: \"add render() returning HTML markup for a frame data-figma-id=\\\"4478:7209\\\" with explicit fixed CSS width:402px and height:874px\"",
          "planContract.plan_items[*].implementation_constraints: \"Frame 4478:7209 must explicitly use box-sizing:border-box, border:0 and padding:0; its geometry must not depend on inherited host styles.\" — no mention of an inline style attribute",
          "scripts/kodjo/lib/vnext-figma-browser-observer.js:81 — generated host injects `<style>html,body{margin:0;padding:0}</style>`, so a stylesheet-based declaration measures identically at getBoundingClientRect and passes PROOF-bb70518aae0e57dbe5f2b7bc",
          "scripts/kodjo/qualify-vnext-figma-real-path.js:110-111 — assertMarkup: `const frame=(html.match(/<[^>]+>/g)||[]).find(tag=>/\\bdata-figma-id\\s*=\\s*([\"'])4478:7209\\1/.test(tag)); const style=frame?.match(/\\bstyle\\s*=\\s*([\"'])(.*?)\\1/); if(!style)throw Error('VNEXT_FIGMA_REAL_DIMENSION_DECLARATIONS_REQUIRED');`",
          "scripts/kodjo/qualify-vnext-figma-real-path.js:112-115 — width/height are read only from the parsed inline `style` declarations of that tag and must match /^(\\d+(?:\\.\\d+)?)px$/ with value 402 / 874",
          "scripts/kodjo/qualify-vnext-figma-real-path.js:118 — assertDelta runs `node -e '(assertMarkup)(require(\"./src/features/example/Screen.js\").render())'` after every delivery and after test execution"
        ],
        "required_correction": "State in implementation_constraints, and mirror in the three Screen.js change intents (CHG-c9625c383df5de1cd29b7051, CHG-4b68fb3d2adf7997aad5936e, CHG-73a13a97d69b4414307b80ff), that width:402px, height:874px, box-sizing:border-box, border:0 and padding:0 must be declared in the inline style attribute of the element bearing data-figma-id=\"4478:7209\", and that <style> blocks, classes or any stylesheet-based declaration do not satisfy the markup contract even when the rendered geometry is exact.",
