\\":\\\"The plan requires \\\\\\\"explicit fixed CSS width:402px and height:874px\\\\\\\" and that frame 4478:7209 \\\\\\\"must explicitly use box-sizing:border-box, border:0 and padding:0\\\\\\\", but no constraint states WHERE those declarations must live. The post-delivery markup gate reads them from one place only: it scans the render() string for the first tag bearing data-figma-id=\\\\\\\"4478:7209\\\\\\\", requires a style=\\\\\\\"...\\\\\\\" attribute ON THAT TAG, and parses width/height from that attribute. A delivery that declares the identical fixed geometry in a <style> block or a CSS class inside the returned markup renders at exactly 402x874 (the host page zeroes html/body margins, so rendered geometry is identical) and therefore satisfies both VISUAL_COMPARE obligations and the rendered-geometry wording of the plan, yet is rejected with VNEXT_FIGMA_REAL_DIMENSION_DECLARATIONS_REQUIRED before any review verdict. The plan as written admits a conforming delivery that the gate refuses.\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":[\\\"scripts/kodjo/qualify-vnext-figma-real-path.js:110-111 — assertMarkup: `const frame=(html.match(/<[^>]+>/g)||[]).find(tag=>/\\\\\\\\bdata-figma-id\\\\\\\\s*=\\\\\\\\s*([\\\\\\\"'])4478:7209\\\\\\\\1/.test(tag)); const style=frame?.match(/\\\\\\\\bstyle\\\\\\\\s*=\\\\\\\\s*([\\\\\\\"'])(.*?)\\\\\\\\1/); if(!style)throw Error('VNEXT_FIGMA_REAL_DIMENSION_DECLARATIONS_REQUIRED');`\\\",\\\"scripts/kodjo/qualify-vnext-figma-real-path.js:112-115 — width/height are read only from the parsed inline `style` declarations of that tag and must match /^(\\\\\\\\d+(?:\\\\\\\\.\\\\\\\\d+)?)px$/ with value 402 / 874\\\",\\\"scripts/kodjo/qualify-vnext-figma-real-path.js:118 — assertDelta runs `node -e '(assertMarkup)(require(\\\\\\\"./src/features/example/Screen.js\\\\\\\").render())'` after every delivery and after test execution\\\",\\\"planContract.plan_items[*].implementation_constraints: \\\\\\\"Frame 4478:7209 must explicitly use box-sizing:border-box, border:0 and padding:0; its geometry must not depend on inherited host styles.\\\\\\\" — no mention of an inline style attribute\\\",\\\"CHG-c9625c383df5de1cd29b7051 / IMP-229b28a0d2ccd5de1d43304c intent: \\\\\\\"add render() returning HTML markup for a frame data-figma-id=\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"4478:7209\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" with explicit fixed CSS width:402px and height:874px\\\\\\\"\\\",\\\"scripts/kodjo/lib/vnext-figma-browser-observer.js:81 — generated host injects `<style>html,body{margin:0;padding:0}</style>`, so a stylesheet-based declaration measures identically at getBoundingClientRect and passes PROOF-bb70518aae0e57dbe5f2b7bc\\\"],\\\"required_correction\\\":\\\"State in implementation_constraints, and mirror in the three Screen.js change intents (CHG-c9625c383df5de1cd29b7051, CHG-4b68fb3d2adf7997aad5936e, CHG-73a13a97d69b4414307b80ff), that width:402px, height:874px, box-sizing:border-box, border:0 and padding:0 must be declared in the inline style attribute of the element bearing data-figma-id=\\\\\\\"4478:7209\\\\\\\", and that <style> blocks, classes or any stylesheet-based declaration do not satisfy the markup contract even when the rendered geometry is exact.\\\",\\\"dependency_target_indices\\\":[226,227,230,412,417,418,419,420,422]},{\\\"category\\\":\\\"TEST_GAP\\\",\\\"target_type\\\":\\\"TEST\\\",\\\"target_id\\\":\\\"TEST-f1b692f59ec2f3530f895873\\\",\\\"finding\\\":\\\"The title obligation says the title data-figma-id=\\\\\\\"4953:6611\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\"contains exactly \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Zones corporelles\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\". Both enforcing gates are strictly stronger than \\\\\\\"contains\\\\\\\": the independent observer returns `title.textContent` and verifyMeasurements compares non-numeric EQUALS values by exact canonical equality (tolerance is never applied to strings), while the markup gate requires the literal adjacency `data-figma-id=\\\\\\\"4953:6611\\\\\\\"[^>]*>Zones corporelles</`. A pretty-printed title (`>\\\\\\\\n  Zones corporelles\\\\\\\\n</h1